---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';

const updated = 'September 29, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Lullaby Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the local-only Lullaby Android app."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>Lullaby Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="post-desc">Effective and last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>
        Lullaby's public Google Play build is free and local-only. A separately
        configured server-enabled build offers an optional encrypted server copy
        for manual backup and transfer. We do not sell, rent, advertise against,
        or share baby care information.
      </p>

      <h2>Information stored by the app</h2>
      <p>Lullaby can store the following information locally on your device:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Child profile names, dates of birth, and avatar/color preferences.</li>
        <li>Feed, sleep, diaper, note, and reminder records.</li>
        <li>Weight, length/height, and head-circumference measurements.</li>
        <li>App preferences such as display units, theme, and quiet hours.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is personal and may be health-related. It remains in the
        app's private storage on your device. Lullaby disables Android cloud backup
        and device-to-device transfer for this data.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect or share</h2>
      <p>
        The local-only Android build does not transmit personal information,
        health information, analytics, advertising identifiers, crash telemetry,
        location, contacts, photos, or usage history.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app has no advertising SDK and does not sell data. Notification
        permission is used only to deliver reminders you configure. The boot
        permission lets Android restore those reminders after a restart.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional server-enabled mode</h2>
      <p>
        A server-enabled build does not upload anything until an adult explicitly
        creates or joins a server copy. A snapshot can include child profiles,
        care logs, growth measurements, reminders, and display preferences.
        Upload and download are manual; Lullaby does not silently merge devices.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each server copy has a random family ID and pairing key. The server stores
        only a hash of the pairing key and encrypts snapshots at rest with
        AES-256-GCM. Anyone with both pairing values can access or replace that
        copy, so they must be kept private. Server mode has no advertising,
        analytics, account directory, or administrator data API.
      </p>

      <h2>User-directed exports</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose Export All Data, export a Health Summary PDF, or use the
        Android share sheet, you choose the destination. The selected receiving
        app or service handles that copy under its own privacy terms. Lullaby
        does not receive a copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention, deletion, and recovery</h2>
      <p>
        Data remains on the device until you edit or delete it, use
        <strong>Settings → Local data & privacy → Delete all local data</strong>,
        clear Android app storage, or uninstall Lullaby.
      </p>
      <p>
        In server-enabled mode, Settings → Server backup → Delete server copy
        permanently removes the remote snapshot. Delete All Local Data also
        attempts remote deletion before resetting the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lullaby has no account-recovery workflow. Local-only data cannot be
        recovered after deletion. In server-enabled mode, a device can download
        a remote snapshot only while that snapshot and its pairing values still
        exist. Export All Data creates a readable JSON archive for your records;
        this release cannot import that archive back into Lullaby.
      </p>

      <h2>Children and intended users</h2>
      <p>
        Lullaby is intended for adults, parents, and caregivers. It is not
        directed to children and does not ask a child to use the app or submit
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Health and medical disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Lullaby organizes information supplied by a caregiver. It is not a
        medical device and does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any medical
        condition. It is not a substitute for advice from a qualified healthcare
        professional.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Android's application sandbox protects local app storage from other apps
        under normal operating conditions. You are responsible for securing the
        device and any files you choose to export.
      </p>

      <h2>Future accounts, sync, and purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts, automatic synchronization, partner collaboration, and paid
        features are not part of the Google Play release. Before enabling those
        features there, we will provide appropriate disclosures and controls and
        update the Google Play Data safety declaration.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when Lullaby changes or legal requirements
        evolve. The effective date above will be updated. Material changes to data
        handling will also be disclosed in the app before they take effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about Lullaby privacy can be sent to
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Lullaby privacy`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        Please do not include baby care records or other sensitive information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
